Regression test: a close request sent to a quick-help tooltip must not crash.

A quick-help tooltip is shown over a work window, then its frame receives SalEvent::Close (what
WM_DELETE_WINDOW on X11 or WM_CLOSE on Windows delivers). Closing ends every help window, so the
tooltip is disposed while the Close handler still uses it; the test expects the tooltip disposed,
the work window kept and no crash.

License: the new test file is HST-owned (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary); the makefile keeps MPL-2.0.
Test: CppunitTest_vcl_lifecycle.
---
--- a/vcl/CppunitTest_vcl_lifecycle.mk
+++ b/vcl/CppunitTest_vcl_lifecycle.mk
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 
 $(eval $(call gb_CppunitTest_add_exception_objects,vcl_lifecycle, \
 	vcl/qa/cppunit/lifecycle \
+	vcl/qa/cppunit/HstHelpWindowClose \
 ))
 
 $(eval $(call gb_CppunitTest_use_externals,vcl_lifecycle,boost_headers))
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vcl/qa/cppunit/HstHelpWindowClose.cxx
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+/* -*- Mode: C++; tab-width: 4; indent-tabs-mode: nil; c-basic-offset: 4; fill-column: 100 -*- */
+/*
